course: dictionary
lesson: 13354
title: Handmade
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Handmade is a word you can work out from its parts: hand and made. Something handmade was made by a person using their hands or simple tools, not by a machine in a factory. «Mia wore a handmade scarf with red and blue stripes.» The stripes were woven by a person, so handmade means made by hand.
explain: Context helps you spot the meaning. «The class made handmade cards for the school fair.» Children making cards in class use their hands and paper, not a machine, so the cards are handmade. Ask yourself: could a machine have made this? If the answer is no, the word probably means handmade.
explain: Handmade things often cost more in shops. «The handmade bowl cost more than the plastic one.» A person needs time to make each handmade item, so fewer can be made in a day. Each handmade thing is usually a little different from the next one.
fact: Handmade means made by a person using their hands or simple tools.
fact: Handmade things are not made by machines in a factory.
fact: «Handmade cards» are cards a person has made by hand.
fact: «Handmade jewellery» is jewellery a person has made by hand, often taking a long time.
fact: Handmade things often cost more because they take time to make.
exercise: «Mia wore a handmade scarf with red and blue stripes.» What does handmade mean? | Very old and cracked | Bought from a big shop in town | Painted by a machine | *Made by a person's hands, not by a factory machine
exercise: «The handmade bowl cost more than the plastic one.» Why might a handmade bowl cost more? | It was made in a huge factory | It was already broken | *A person needed time to make it | It was made of plastic
exercise: «The class made handmade cards for the school fair.» Find and copy the word that tells you the cards were made by hand. | class | *handmade | school | fair
test: «Each handmade mug in the shop is a little different from the others.» Why is each mug a little different? | *Because a person made each one by hand | Because they are all the same colour | Because the shop lost some of them | Because they are very old
test: «Grandad's handmade chair took weeks to build, using only a saw, a hammer and his hands.» What does handmade show about the chair? | *It was made by a person with simple tools | It was found in a field | It was bought from a shop | It was made by a machine in a factory
exam: «Jade bought a handmade necklace at the market, and it was not like the ones in the big shops.» What does handmade mean in this sentence? | Made in a factory | Bought from a big shop | Made from plastic by a machine | *Made by a person's hands, so each one is a little different
